# Rebuild the double-clickable app

After any change that affects the app (code, Info.plist, resources, Makefile):

1. Rebuild with `make codesign` (bumps `CFBundleVersion` and produces `.build/release/CCTV-<n>.app`).
2. Do **not** copy the app to Desktop or elsewhere unless asked.
3. Leave the double-clickable bundle at `.build/release/CCTV-<n>.app` (number matches the build).

## Versioning

- Bump **build number** (`CFBundleVersion`) on every rebuild — not the marketing version.
- Keep `CFBundleShortVersionString` (e.g. `0.3.0`) for intentional releases only.
- The Makefile increments the build number automatically during `bundle` / `codesign`, and
  stamps it into `CFBundleDisplayName` (`CCTV n`), `CFBundleIdentifier`
  (`co.uk.dannyhope.cctv.n`), and the `.app` filename so TCC / Finder don’t confuse builds.
